content.text:
Nothing there. So the fix is to add an explicit shell + environment override to your settings.json. This tells LaTeX Workshop exactly which shell to spawn and what env to give it:

```json
"latex-workshop.latex.tools": [
 {
    "name": "pdflatex",
    "command": "/usr/local/texlive/2022/bin/universal-darwin/pdflatex",
    "args": ["-synctex=1", "-interaction=nonstopmode", "-file-line-error", "%DOC%"]
  }
],
"latex-workshop.latex.recipes": [
  {
    "name": "pdflatex",
    "tools": ["pdflatex"]
  }
]
```

But before I edit anything, let me try the simplest possible fix first — add an env key to your settings.json that explicitly prepends TeX to the PATH for LaTeX Workshop's subprocesses. This is one line and won't disturb anything else:

input.old_string:
"latex-workshop.latex.recipes": [
        {
            "name": "latexmk",
            "tools": [
                "latexmk"
            ]
        },

"env": {
                "PATH" : "/usr/local/texlive/2022/bin/universal-darwin"
            }

